  "findings": [
    "The claimed Java account is largely correct at the final SVG backend stage. UFontImpl#getFamily does quote normalization and SansSerif canonicalization, while SvgGraphics#text performs the actual Monospaced->monospace rewrite and only then applies NBSP conversion for monospace or Courier.",
    "The reviewed production diff in 336db230 is narrow and non-fixture-shaped. It centralizes logical Monospaced canonicalization in text_render::write_text_element and leaves quoted-family behavior alone, which the passing checker_sequence_quoted_monospaced_defaultfont case confirms.",
    "Base-family paths behave as claimed on fresh inputs: component labels with mixed-case Monospaced and state arrows with Courier both match Java exactly through diff_one --no-oracle, and the preserved checker_monospaced_lr_dpi evidence case now passes.",
    "The mechanism fails on inline <font:...> families because Rust still has an upstream scope gap in creole::handle_tag. For every <font:Name> tag it sets nested.monospace = true unconditionally, so push_literal converts spaces to NBSP before text_render sees the finalized family. Java does not do that; it keeps Courier New spaces literal.",
    "That gap is executable on a fresh sequence-message counterexample. checker_sequence_inline_arrow_family_matrix_scale is valid Java input, preserves both Java SVG and product-path Rust output, and fails solely because Rust emits NBSP-expanded Courier New text and the resulting wider width perturbs layout.",
    "A second fresh sequence counterexample, checker_sequence_inline_family_matrix_scale, fails for the same reason in the note segment, so the bug is not confined to one exact line shape.",
    "I also found a broader valid failure in checker_inline_font_family_matrix_note, where Java renders a note-only diagram as CLASS while Rust renders DESCRIPTION. That failure is adjacent rather than the primary causal disproof, but under the T14 rule it still remains preserved executable drift."
  ],
