  "verdict_reason": "I found fresh valid no-oracle counterexamples that disprove the mechanism's claimed inline-family coverage. Base-family Monospaced and Courier serialization now match Java, but inline <font:Courier New> still takes the Rust monospace spacing path, producing NBSP-expanded text and wider geometry on fresh sequence inputs. Under the T14 checker rule, those valid preserved failures reject the change."
